WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.858
In this video you will record one water
measurement, start to finish.

00:00:04.978 --> 00:00:10.210
You will choose a station, type the depth to
water, add water quality and a note,

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:13.018
then save and find it on your list.

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:16.802
To start, look at the menu on the left.

00:00:16.922 --> 00:00:19.394
Add a measurement starts a new one.

00:00:20.217 --> 00:00:22.089
Click it.

00:00:22.209 --> 00:00:25.353
The form opens small, with two boxes.

00:00:25.473 --> 00:00:28.185
Choose a station and the rest appears.

00:00:28.305 --> 00:00:30.969
Save stays grey until you do.

00:00:31.783 --> 00:00:34.567
This box filters stations by type.

00:00:34.687 --> 00:00:38.503
With many stations, pick a type to shorten the
list.

00:00:38.623 --> 00:00:41.095
We will leave it on All types.

00:00:41.917 --> 00:00:44.125
Now click the Station box.

00:00:44.245 --> 00:00:46.429
Your stations drop down.

00:00:46.549 --> 00:00:50.701
With many stations, type part of a name or
code to search.

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:53.869
Choose Asha's open well.

00:00:53.989 --> 00:00:59.293
The title now says Add a groundwater well
measurement, and the rest of the form appears.

00:01:00.117 --> 00:01:02.685
Station type is filled in for you.

00:01:02.805 --> 00:01:06.069
It decides which measures the form asks for.

00:01:06.883 --> 00:01:09.259
Next, date and time.

00:01:09.379 --> 00:01:11.251
They start as now.

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:14.347
If you measured earlier, change them here.

00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:16.579
They cannot be in the future.

00:01:17.383 --> 00:01:21.175
Location comes from the station, so you never
type it.

00:01:21.295 --> 00:01:24.343
It shows the well's latitude and longitude.

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:27.022
What did you record?

00:01:27.142 --> 00:01:29.854
Each round button is one kind of measure.

00:01:29.974 --> 00:01:32.446
Groundwater depth is already on.

00:01:32.566 --> 00:01:38.758
You can add Temperature, Water quality, a
Photo, a Video, or Scan for sensors.

00:01:39.583 --> 00:01:41.599
This is the main box.

00:01:41.719 --> 00:01:44.959
It asks for Groundwater depth, in metres.

00:01:45.079 --> 00:01:47.311
The unit shows in brackets.

00:01:48.117 --> 00:01:51.237
Depth to water is how far down the water is.

00:01:51.357 --> 00:01:56.253
Measure from the ground, or the marked point
on the well rim, down to the water.

00:01:56.373 --> 00:01:58.965
A bigger number means deeper water.

00:01:59.783 --> 00:02:05.903
Type a number that looks wrong, like nine hundred,
and a yellow note says this value looks unusual.

00:02:06.023 --> 00:02:07.943
It is only a warning.

00:02:08.063 --> 00:02:10.031
You can still save.

00:02:10.850 --> 00:02:13.154
Click Save with the box empty.

00:02:13.274 --> 00:02:18.530
OurWater asks for at least one value, or a
photo, and does not save.

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:21.486
Letters do not work either.

00:02:21.606 --> 00:02:27.054
Type abc and press Save, and OurWater says
which box needs a number.

00:02:27.883 --> 00:02:30.499
Let us start again, properly.

00:02:30.619 --> 00:02:37.123
The form now opens with Asha's open well already
chosen, as when you scan a station's QR code.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:39.822
Type the depth.

00:02:39.942 --> 00:02:44.286
In Asha's well, the water is eleven point nine
metres down.

00:02:45.117 --> 00:02:48.405
To add another measure, click its round
button.

00:02:48.525 --> 00:02:51.645
Click Temperature, and a new box opens.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:56.266
Type the temperature of the water, in degrees
Celsius.

00:02:56.386 --> 00:02:58.618
We will say twenty-six.

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:01.370
Now water quality.

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:04.802
Click this button to open a panel of test
results.

00:03:05.617 --> 00:03:08.521
Tested the water with a strip or a pen?

00:03:08.641 --> 00:03:11.209
Fill only the boxes you measured.

00:03:11.329 --> 00:03:13.201
Leave the rest empty.

00:03:13.321 --> 00:03:15.697
It all saves as one sample.

00:03:16.517 --> 00:03:20.189
pH tells you if water is acid or alkaline.

00:03:20.309 --> 00:03:22.277
Seven is in the middle.

00:03:22.397 --> 00:03:24.413
Type seven point four.

00:03:25.217 --> 00:03:30.905
Total dissolved solids, in milligrams per
litre, is how much is dissolved in the water.

00:03:31.025 --> 00:03:33.089
Type three hundred twenty.

00:03:33.917 --> 00:03:37.829
Photo adds a picture, perhaps of the gauge or
the water.

00:03:37.949 --> 00:03:41.741
Take one with the camera, or choose one from
your device.

00:03:41.861 --> 00:03:44.069
A short caption is optional.

00:03:44.883 --> 00:03:48.579
Video records up to ten seconds, with sound.

00:03:48.699 --> 00:03:52.851
It is made smaller before sending, so it
uploads quickly.

00:03:52.971 --> 00:03:55.107
We will not add one now.

00:03:55.917 --> 00:03:57.789
Notes are optional.

00:03:57.909 --> 00:04:00.861
Write anything the next person should know.

00:04:00.981 --> 00:04:05.085
Here: the water is clear, and where we
measured from.

00:04:05.917 --> 00:04:11.149
Everything looks right: depth, temperature,
and two water quality values.

00:04:11.269 --> 00:04:13.141
Click Save measurement.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:17.070
OurWater takes you to your list for this
station.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:21.102
One visit made four rows, one for each value.

00:04:21.222 --> 00:04:23.454
The new rows are at the top.

00:04:24.283 --> 00:04:29.755
Each row shows the station, measure, value and
unit, and time.

00:04:29.875 --> 00:04:31.747
Made a mistake?

00:04:31.867 --> 00:04:34.987
Edit, at the row's end, fixes it.

00:04:35.817 --> 00:04:39.105
Every kind of station asks for different
measures.

00:04:39.225 --> 00:04:44.745
A rain gauge leads with Rainfall, in
millimetres, and has no Water quality button.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:51.718
A check dam leads with Water level, and also offers
Rainfall, Temperature and Water quality.

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:55.070
That is how you record a measurement.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:05:00.302
Choose the station, type the main value, add
the rest, and press Save.

00:05:00.422 --> 00:05:03.086
Thanks for helping look after our water.
